	spec: "The web obeys /toggle (task ghs) and Ctrl-O like the terminal: the same targets, ranges, kinds and dialog. A /toggle from the host flips the card as a click does, with the same animation. Ctrl-O calls preventDefault so the browser's open-file action does not run. Closing the block that the URL hash names (#t45) removes the hash from the URL without adding a history entry. Web cards keep their own fold presentation; the 200-row limit for open terminal results does not apply to the web. Open plain prompt and assistant cards expose an accessible timestamp collapse button, including background completion prompts; selecting or tapping prose does not collapse them. The entire web card header, including its label, toggles a closable card even while its text is selected; prose retains text-selection behavior. Background Bash completion reports show command exit status, not message-delivery/read receipts. Automatic background Bash completion reports are folding cards, like tool results: they start collapsed, open through their header, and close through their header or unselected output. Links retain navigation and selected output retains selection. Normal human prompts retain their open-by-default behavior.",
